{
    "$comment": "Scenarios of run-commands.sh. `route` is the name the routing table (`bin/route.mjs`) knows the command by; `family` picks the fixture state (base: untouched workspace; warm: task cache filled by a Node run; runs: one recorded run in .vis/runs); `scales` runs the scenario for every --sizes value, otherwise only for the default size; `stubs` puts stand-in package managers on PATH (so no network and no real install runs); `handoff` gives the bare binary the environment the launcher sets (a binary started without it hands `run` to Node); `mode` is a late-miss or cold run; `compare` is how output is compared with Node (exact; sorted lines where the order of interleaved lines may differ; exit: only the exit code, where the binary hands the command to the package manager and Node does not); `label` tells the run scenarios apart; `comparatorFixture` plain is a non-workspace project (some comparators cannot find a bin in a workspace root); `comparators` are real tools run in a separate copy of the fixture, with the real PATH; `floor` is the stand-in package manager run directly (the spawn cost the command cannot go below).",
